+grounding:
+  - id: G1
+    principle: "A template defines the SHAPE of an output artifact. It must not define which artifacts get produced (play/skill contract) or rules for artifact content (rules/)."
+    source: "main:core/components/memory/standards/templates/_index.md  § 'When to Add Here'"
+  - id: G2
+    principle: "Layout: rules/ = how an artifact must be structured and enforced; templates/ = what the final output looks like. 'plan.md - rules for execution plans' is already listed as a deferred rules/ follow-up."
+    source: "main:core/components/memory/standards/_index.md § 'Layout principle'; main:core/components/memory/standards/rules/_index.md § 'Deferred follow-ups'"
+  - id: G3
+    principle: "Template index rows name the concrete skills/agents that instantiate the template, and a template must be instantiated by at least one skill or play."
+    source: "main:core/components/memory/standards/templates/_index.md (Consumers column of every existing row; 'When to Add Here' bullet 2)"
+  - id: G4
+    principle: "'plan' already names a build-plan DAG of file-level pieces (implement writes specs/implement/plan.yaml via author-build-plan); 'checkpoint' already names the human approval gate (Tether/Orbit/Vanish) with its own template."
+    source: "main:core/components/plays/implement/SKILL.md (plan.yaml, author-build-plan); main:core/components/memory/standards/templates/checkpoint.md; main:core/components/memory/standards/rules/_index.md (deferred plan.md = 'DAG, file-level changes, tests')"
+  - id: G5
+    principle: "Platform tool docs (tools/github, tools/gitlab) are paired KB narratives that mirror each other: platform differences for a verb are stated in BOTH docs and cross-referenced (attach-sub-issue points to the GitLab reference; gitlab view-issue states the closed_at difference)."
+    source: "main:core/components/memory/tools/github/adapter.md § attach-sub-issue; main:core/components/memory/tools/gitlab/adapter.md § view-issue"
+  - id: G6
+    principle: "Existing templates are timeless canonical shapes: no issue-in-progress notes, no 'will be updated' prose; any provenance is a stated work context, not a live design status."
+    source: "main:core/components/memory/standards/templates/{pr-body,commit-message,checkpoint,github-issue,knowledge-file}.md (read in full)"
+  - id: G7
+    principle: "Work-kind vocabulary: Business Intent, Feature, Story (a Task), Bug, Spike, Chore."
+    source: "main:.garura/user-provided/managing-work.md (kinds table)"
+  - id: G8
+    principle: "STM structure is limited to specs/evidence/checkpoint/context/review; plans under specs/ are allowed. stm.base-path ends in a slash."
+    source: ".garura/core/config.yaml (ADR 017 comment on structure keys; stm.base-path: .garura/project/issues/)"
+
+conformant:
+  - "templates/plan.md front-matter `kind` list matches the work kinds on main (G7) plus drive/play (Drive is defined in main glossary / ADR 029)."
+  - "templates/plan.md lives at {stm_base}{issue}/specs/plan.md - inside a permitted STM key (G8); {stm_base}{issue} without a slash is correct given the base-path value."
+  - "templates/plan.md has a concrete instantiating skill (manage-plan, added in the same branch), so the 'instantiated by at least one skill' entry test (G3) is met."
+  - "templates/_index.md row is placed in the Contents table and the template is plain-language, consistent with user-facing-voice (templates are exempt anyway per main:rules/user-facing-voice.md Scope)."
+  - "tools/github/adapter.md view-issue edit stays descriptive (executable commands live in verbs.md, per its own Overview) and the field list matches verbs.md and `gh issue view --json` available fields (checked locally on gh 2.102)."
