+findings:
+  - id: M1
+    severity: P3
+    file: core/components/memory/standards/templates/plan.md
+    lines: "intro paragraph; '## Rules' items 5, 6, 8"
+    principle: "G1, G2 - a template carries shape, not contract or lifecycle policy."
+    basis: >
+      The template opens with "Every drive and every play writes one before it works, keeps it up
+      to date while it works, and is done only when its plan is done", and Rules 5 (kept current),
+      6 (every plan names what it serves) and 8 ("done means the plan is done") decide WHICH work
+      must produce the artifact and WHEN it is done. templates/_index 'When to Add Here' says a
+      file does NOT belong in templates/ if it "defines WHICH artifacts to produce (that's play /
+      skill contract territory)" or "defines rules for artifact content (that's rules/)", and
+      rules/_index already reserves `plan.md` there as a deferred follow-up. Rules 1-4 and 7 are
+      legitimate field rules (cf. pr-body 'Field Rules'); 5, 6, 8 are not.
+    suggested_fix: "Keep the shape + field rules in templates/plan.md; move the lifecycle rules (kept current, serves-chain, done-means-plan-done) to rules/plan.md or the manage-plan / play contract, and link from the template under a '## Related' section as base templates do."
