+      tool doc and adds a 'Gap: GitLab carries no equivalent' note to platform-adapter/reference/
+      gitlab/verbs.md, but main:tools/gitlab/adapter.md § view-issue (which documents the
+      closed_at difference) is left untouched. Callers reading the KB narrative for GitLab get no
+      warning that the issue tree is GitHub-only, unlike attach-sub-issue where the GitHub doc
+      cross-references the GitLab fallback.
+    suggested_fix: "Add one sentence to tools/gitlab/adapter.md view-issue: no type/parent/sub-issue fields; issue-tree callers are GitHub-only."
+    taxonomy_row: none (bucket definition)
+
+  - id: M6
+    severity: P3
+    file: core/components/memory/tools/github/adapter.md
+    lines: "view-issue: 'they need gh 2.94.0 or newer'"
+    principle: "G5 (tool docs state verb semantics and caveats) + no prior minimum-version contract on main."
+    basis: >
+      `git grep` on main finds no stated minimum gh version anywhere in core/ or docs/ (checked
+      patterns for 'gh version', 'gh >=', 'minimum ... gh'). The doc now introduces a first
+      hard prerequisite, but only inside one verb's prose, and the paired verbs.md says an older gh
+      "rejects these fields" - meaning the whole view-issue call fails (it is one --json list), not
+      just the tree fields, for every play that reads issues (archive bucketing uses closedAt).
+      The memory doc does not say where the prerequisite is declared (install/doctor check) or
+      what a caller should do on an older gh. The runtime breakage itself belongs to the
+      harness/code reviewers (potentially P2 as a breaking verb contract); this finding covers
+      only the missing documentation of the prerequisite.
+    suggested_fix: "Say where the gh minimum is enforced (install-garura / preflight) and the expected failure mode, or make the tree fields a separate verb/opt-in so existing view-issue callers keep working on older gh."
+    taxonomy_row: none (bucket definition)
+    cross_category_note: "Hand to executable-code / harness review: four platform_adapter.py copies now request the new fields unconditionally."
+
+  - id: M7
+    severity: P4
+    file: core/components/memory/standards/templates/plan.md
+    lines: "front matter `now:`; Rule 4 ('\"Now\" is always set'); Rule 8; `status: {active | done | dropped}`"
+    principle: "Template internal precision (field rules must say what a field holds in every allowed state) - cf. main:templates/checkpoint.md, which marks nullable fields (`decision: null | ...`)."
+    basis: >
+      `status: done|dropped` is allowed but Rule 4 says `now` is always set, and no item can be
+      'now' in a finished plan; Rule 8 defines done for the issue but not what a `dropped` plan
+      means or how `now` reads then. The base checkpoint template states null-able fields
+      explicitly.
+    suggested_fix: "Write `now: {item number | null when status is done or dropped}` and adjust Rule 4 to 'while active'."
+    taxonomy_row: none (bucket definition)
